  "kind": "place",
  "title": "Mehrgarh Neolithic settlement",
  "summary": "Mehrgarh, mounds on the Kachi plain near the Bolan Pass in Balochistan, holds one of the earliest farming settlements of the north-west Indian subcontinent. Its Neolithic residents grew mostly barley with some wheat and domesticated cattle. Sources date the start from about 8500 to 6500 BCE; the excavators' chronology begins the Aceramic Neolithic around 6500 BCE.",
